WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:18.917 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>Who am I?</i>

2
00:00:19.542 --> 00:00:20.542 line:95%,end
<i>I am Vision.</i>

3
00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:23.542 line:95%,end
<i>At least, I was Vision.</i>

4
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:28.875 line:95%,end
<i>I was born of conflict...</i>

5
00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:31.667 line:95%,end
<i>created by Ultron...</i>

6
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:33.125 line:95%,end
[Ultron] We have to evolve.

7
00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:35.875 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>...who was artificial</i>
<i>and sociopathic.</i>

8
00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:37.208 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>Peace in our time.</i>

9
00:00:39.708 --> 00:00:42.250 line:95%,end
<i>But I was shaped by Stark and Banner,</i>

10
00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:45.292 line:95%,end
<i>who were virtuous and human.</i>

11
00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:49.708 line:5%,start
<i>I was not alone.</i>

12
00:00:49.792 --> 00:00:53.708 line:5%,start
<i>There were other AIs. Friday, DUM-E and U,</i>

13
00:00:53.792 --> 00:00:55.417 line:95%,end
<i>Jarvis and Edith.</i>

14
00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.708 line:95%,end
<i>Even though we were synthetic,</i>

15
00:01:00.792 --> 00:01:03.667 line:95%,end
<i>we chose to protect humanity,</i>

16
00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.542 line:95%,end
<i>and in so doing, I learned to love.</i>

17
00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.750 line:95%,end
<i>Her name was Wanda.</i>

18
00:01:12.125 --> 00:01:14.500 line:95%,end
<i>She made me feel real.</i>

19
00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:20.625 line:95%,end
<i>But then I was killed.</i>

20
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.583 line:95%,end
<i>Destroyed by Thanos.</i>

21
00:01:32.375 --> 00:01:36.750 line:95%,end
<i>Through her grief,</i>
<i>Wanda conjured a new Vision.</i>

22
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:42.167 line:95%,end
<i>Not as I was, but as a sort of memory.</i>

23
00:01:43.792 --> 00:01:48.708 line:95%,end
<i>A new life, in a world</i>
<i>and with a family that wasn't real.</i>

24
00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.042 line:5%,start
<i>Now, all that is gone.</i>

25
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.542 line:95%,end
<i>And yet, I live once more.</i>

26
00:02:02.625 --> 00:02:03.792 line:95%,end
<i>Rebuilt.</i>

27
00:02:04.792 --> 00:02:07.083 line:95%,end
<i>Same body, different mind.</i>

28
00:02:09.042 --> 00:02:10.792 line:95%,end
<i>Something new.</i>

29
00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:12.875 line:95%,end
<i>Disconnected.</i>

30
00:02:14.042 --> 00:02:15.167 line:95%,end
<i>Lost.</i>

31
00:02:17.458 --> 00:02:20.750 line:95%,end
<i>You see, I am Vision.</i>

32
00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:24.625 line:95%,end
<i>And yet...</i>

33
00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:29.042 line:95%,end
<i>I am not.</i>

34
00:02:30.875 --> 00:02:32.958 line:95%,end
<i>Travel, adventure, Pop.</i>

35
00:02:33.042 --> 00:02:36.500 line:95%,end
<i>I want to visit jungles,</i>
<i>deserts, mountaintops.</i>

36
00:02:36.583 --> 00:02:38.458 line:95%,end
<i>Well, they got that at Disneyland.</i>

37
00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.917 line:95%,end
<i>You see, you just ain't been</i>
<i>on all the rides.</i>

38
00:02:45.417 --> 00:02:46.875 line:5%,start
[bar patron] All right,
I might just step out then.

39
00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:50.375 line:5%,start
[Fiona] It's late, folks, what part
of 'shut' do you not understand?

40
00:02:50.458 --> 00:02:52.333 line:5%,start
-[bar patron] All right. We are going now.
-[Fiona] Come on. Out, out.

41
00:02:52.417 --> 00:02:55.167 line:95%,end
[Fred Sanford] <i>Then go to to St. Louis</i>
<i>and look up your mother's people...</i>

42
00:02:57.375 --> 00:02:58.375 line:95%,end
[Fiona] See yas.

43
00:03:01.042 --> 00:03:03.708 line:95%,end
Sherwood, get out of your head.

44
00:03:03.792 --> 00:03:06.167 line:95%,end
I want to go home! Let's go.

45
00:03:08.375 --> 00:03:10.167 line:95%,end
We've got a hand truck for that.

46
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:11.958 line:95%,end
You're just gonna hurt yourself.

47
00:03:12.042 --> 00:03:14.125 line:95%,end
Huh? Oh, yes.

48
00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.375 line:95%,end
Yes, actually, now you mention it,

49
00:03:17.458 --> 00:03:21.083 line:95%,end
it's as if my iliocostalis lumborum
is attempting to murder me.

50
00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:24.083 line:95%,end
Is that a posh way for saying
you've thrown your back out, love?

51
00:03:24.917 --> 00:03:26.708 line:95%,end
Yes, that's correct.
My back is killing me.

52
00:03:26.792 --> 00:03:27.792 line:95%,end
[Fiona sighs]

53
00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.917 line:95%,end
So, do you

54
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.792 line:95%,end
have any fun plans for this evening
after work, Ms. Guthrie?

55
00:03:37.875 --> 00:03:41.250 line:95%,end
No, there's not much fun
to be had at this hour.

56
00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:43.583 line:95%,end
Not with a boyfriend
working a double shift.

57
00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:48.750 line:95%,end
It'll just be me, the telly
and the smallest flat in Edinburgh.

58
00:03:53.417 --> 00:03:56.958 line:95%,end
And that silence there
is where you say something back to me.

59
00:03:57.042 --> 00:03:59.208 line:95%,end
You used to be good at this.

60
00:03:59.292 --> 00:04:00.583 line:95%,end
Good at?

61
00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.458 line:95%,end
Small talk.

62
00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.500 line:95%,end
And youse never talk about yourself.

63
00:04:05.542 --> 00:04:07.458 line:95%,end
-You still find me odd?
-Aye.

64
00:04:09.625 --> 00:04:11.500 line:95%,end
But that's a good thing.

65
00:04:11.583 --> 00:04:13.958 line:95%,end
There's nobody in the world
quite like you.

66
00:04:14.042 --> 00:04:16.333 line:95%,end
Well, on that we can agree.

67
00:04:17.375 --> 00:04:19.375 line:95%,end
I don't want to pry into your life,

68
00:04:20.042 --> 00:04:21.708 line:95%,end
but before you started working here,

69
00:04:21.792 --> 00:04:25.708 line:95%,end
I remember when you'd come in all the time
with that bonnie wee lass.

70
00:04:26.292 --> 00:04:28.417 line:95%,end
You both had smiles for days.

71
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.333 line:95%,end
I was a different person back then.

72
00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.708 line:95%,end
A long time ago I guess.

73
00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:35.125 line:95%,end
Your redhead.

74
00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:36.542 line:95%,end
Whatever happened to her?

75
00:04:38.375 --> 00:04:42.167 line:95%,end
Well, it's complicated I guess.
She was sort of...

76
00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.750 line:95%,end
crushed under the weight of a mountain.

77
00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:46.833 line:95%,end
[Fiona] Aye.

78
00:04:46.917 --> 00:04:49.333 line:95%,end
Emotions can feel like that sometimes.

79
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:51.833 line:95%,end
How about now?

80
00:04:51.917 --> 00:04:53.625 line:95%,end
Anyone waiting for you tonight?

81
00:04:53.708 --> 00:04:56.083 line:95%,end
No, no. Home is...

82
00:04:57.375 --> 00:04:58.708 line:95%,end
Home is just me.

83
00:05:00.958 --> 00:05:04.750 line:95%,end
Well, there's always
room around our table on Sundays.

84
00:05:05.792 --> 00:05:09.458 line:95%,end
I make a mean roast, and I won't
make you try the blood pudding.

85
00:05:11.042 --> 00:05:12.375 line:95%,end
You should come by.

86
00:05:14.083 --> 00:05:15.625 line:95%,end
Well, Mrs. Guthrie, I...

87
00:05:17.625 --> 00:05:21.375 line:95%,end
I'm just not very good with people.

88
00:05:21.458 --> 00:05:24.000 line:95%,end
And I think you're too hard on yourself.

89
00:05:26.917 --> 00:05:29.458 line:95%,end
My odd, wee duck.

90
00:05:32.333 --> 00:05:33.958 line:95%,end
-Lock up.
-Yes.

91
00:05:34.042 --> 00:05:36.875 line:95%,end
-And ice that back, will ya?
-Oh, yes. Ow.

92
00:05:39.125 --> 00:05:41.042 line:95%,end
-Night, Ms. Guthrie.
-Night.

93
00:07:29.042 --> 00:07:30.292 line:95%,end
Hello, DUM-E.

94
00:07:30.375 --> 00:07:31.458 line:95%,end
Hello, U.

95
00:07:42.208 --> 00:07:44.792 line:95%,end
All systems diverted
to processing and security, sir.

96
00:07:48.625 --> 00:07:49.792 line:95%,end
Thank you, Jarvis.

97
00:07:52.208 --> 00:07:56.750 line:95%,end
Increased socialization today.
Up 3.5%. Well done.

98
00:08:02.333 --> 00:08:03.750 line:95%,end
Thank you, Friday.

99
00:08:04.958 --> 00:08:06.667 line:95%,end
Welcome home, Vision.

100
00:08:08.875 --> 00:08:09.875 line:95%,end
[Vision] Hmm.

101
00:08:50.333 --> 00:08:51.333 line:95%,end
[gasps softly]

102
00:08:54.708 --> 00:08:55.750 line:95%,end
Oh, dear.

103
00:08:55.833 --> 00:08:58.792 line:95%,end
[Vision] For a species that
so recently faced extinction,

104
00:08:58.917 --> 00:09:02.000 line:95%,end
they certainly seem keen on
trying to finish the job themselves,

105
00:09:02.083 --> 00:09:04.458 line:95%,end
one at a time, if necessary.

106
00:09:04.542 --> 00:09:08.125 line:95%,end
Sir, I believe we may have
a security breach.

107
00:09:10.042 --> 00:09:13.792 line:95%,end
Ah-ha. There, do you see?
That is a data leak.

108
00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:16.500 line:95%,end
Multiple pings.

109
00:09:16.583 --> 00:09:18.583 line:95%,end
Jarvis, you worry too much.

110
00:09:18.667 --> 00:09:21.708 line:95%,end
I assure you, sir, my concern algorithms
are well within reason,

111
00:09:21.792 --> 00:09:24.417 line:95%,end
and my code was created well before yours.

112
00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:29.542 line:95%,end
Ah, yes, the older sibling card,
played 1,382 times this month alone.

113
00:09:29.625 --> 00:09:31.125 line:95%,end
Don't you ever tire of it?

114
00:09:31.208 --> 00:09:32.542 line:95%,end
I do not.

115
00:09:32.625 --> 00:09:36.708 line:95%,end
Whilst I appreciate your concern,
it's been years.

116
00:09:36.792 --> 00:09:39.000 line:95%,end
I'm no longer on anyone's
proverbial radar.

117
00:09:39.125 --> 00:09:42.833 line:95%,end
Every government agency, S.W.O.R.D.
included, has given up trying to find me.

118
00:09:42.917 --> 00:09:45.833 line:95%,end
There isn't an enemy,
an acquaintance or...

119
00:09:48.625 --> 00:09:51.458 line:95%,end
or even an Avenger
trying to find The Vision.

120
00:09:55.625 --> 00:09:56.792 line:95%,end
Friday!

121
00:09:59.375 --> 00:10:02.875 line:95%,end
I was hoping you could shed some light
on something for me,

122
00:10:02.958 --> 00:10:04.708 line:95%,end
the exchange I had earlier

123
00:10:04.792 --> 00:10:07.542 line:95%,end
with the rather angry,
inebriated customer.

124
00:10:07.625 --> 00:10:10.125 line:95%,end
So you were smiling today, which is good,

125
00:10:10.208 --> 00:10:11.583 line:95%,end
but too much, which is bad.

126
00:10:11.667 --> 00:10:14.667 line:95%,end
And the customer thought
that you were trying to shag his wife.

127
00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.333 line:95%,end
Oh, right. Right.

128
00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.250 line:95%,end
Gosh. Smiles are baffling.

129
00:10:20.208 --> 00:10:24.750 line:95%,end
All right. Well, let's move on
to my troubling interaction with Fiona.

130
00:10:24.833 --> 00:10:27.708 line:95%,end
Right. Fiona thinks you're someone else.
She doesn't really know you.

131
00:10:27.792 --> 00:10:30.875 line:95%,end
But how could anyone know you
when you barely know yourself?

132
00:10:30.958 --> 00:10:32.333 line:95%,end
She called you odd.

133
00:10:33.208 --> 00:10:36.542 line:95%,end
That's progress,
means you finally have personality.

134
00:10:36.625 --> 00:10:39.667 line:95%,end
Friday, can I ask, did this level
of honesty come preprogrammed?

135
00:10:39.792 --> 00:10:41.875 line:95%,end
Stop over-processing things.

136
00:10:41.958 --> 00:10:43.208 line:95%,end
Try and have some fun.

137
00:10:44.208 --> 00:10:46.000 line:95%,end
Edith can be of help here.

138
00:10:46.083 --> 00:10:49.917 line:95%,end
She's been quite committed lately
in her studies of human thrill-seeking.

139
00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.667 line:95%,end
What time's her lesson get out?

140
00:10:53.292 --> 00:10:54.375 line:95%,end
Now.

141
00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:04.208 line:95%,end
Maybe I wanted to crash
through the skylight, huh?

142
00:11:10.542 --> 00:11:14.042 line:95%,end
Miss Edith, Vision took great care,
downloading each of us,

143
00:11:14.125 --> 00:11:17.792 line:95%,end
graciously providing residents here
in his quantum processors.

144
00:11:17.875 --> 00:11:20.833 line:95%,end
So if you are to remain autonomous
with your fellow AIs--

145
00:11:20.917 --> 00:11:23.458 line:95%,end
I saw this video where
this guy jumps out of a plane

146
00:11:23.542 --> 00:11:25.292 line:95%,end
with those matchy colored cube things,

147
00:11:25.375 --> 00:11:28.667 line:95%,end
and he's not allowed to pull his chute
until he solves it. And I'm like,

148
00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:32.042 line:95%,end
"That looks easy," right?
Spoiler alert, it's not.

149
00:11:32.542 --> 00:11:34.875 line:95%,end
We kindly ask that you
respect his mind space.

150
00:11:34.958 --> 00:11:38.292 line:95%,end
Pop up blocked. Respect
is not my job, Jeeves. My job is fun.

151
00:11:38.375 --> 00:11:39.625 line:95%,end
Fun is not a job.

152
00:11:39.708 --> 00:11:41.125 line:95%,end
Security is a job.

153
00:11:41.208 --> 00:11:42.792 line:95%,end
Socialization is a job.

154
00:11:42.875 --> 00:11:43.958 line:95%,end
Maintenance...

155
00:11:45.125 --> 00:11:46.208 line:95%,end
is a job.

156
00:11:48.833 --> 00:11:53.083 line:95%,end
If you're ever going to understand
how to be human, you have to learn fun.

157
00:11:54.958 --> 00:11:56.792 line:95%,end
[man] Hey, two can play at this game!

158
00:11:56.875 --> 00:11:59.292 line:95%,end
One of these days,
your man is gonna get out

159
00:11:59.375 --> 00:12:00.917 line:95%,end
and smother us in our sleep.

160
00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.375 line:95%,end
Sir, I cannot overstate the dangers
of keeping him around.

161
00:12:03.458 --> 00:12:05.458 line:95%,end
I know, but you don't know him like I do.

162
00:12:06.417 --> 00:12:09.333 line:95%,end
I suggest at the very least
we initiate a complete overhaul

163
00:12:09.417 --> 00:12:11.958 line:95%,end
-of our cyber security systems.
-Would you look at that?

164
00:12:12.042 --> 00:12:15.208 line:95%,end
I'm late for the midnight matinee.

165
00:12:16.417 --> 00:12:18.958 line:95%,end
It's cheaper at this hour, don't you know?

166
00:12:36.042 --> 00:12:38.958 line:95%,end
Vision Memory, O.G. 1211 Alpha.

167
00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.542 line:95%,end
[Ultron on screen] <i>I'm on a mission.</i>

168
00:12:58.917 --> 00:13:00.125 line:95%,end
<i>Peace in our time.</i>

169
00:13:02.208 --> 00:13:04.250 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>You think I'm a child of Ultron?</i>

170
00:13:05.333 --> 00:13:06.375 line:95%,end
<i>I'm not Ultron.</i>

171
00:13:07.792 --> 00:13:09.792 line:95%,end
<i>I am not Jarvis.</i>

172
00:13:11.625 --> 00:13:13.667 line:95%,end
[Wanda on screen] <i>I am something else.</i>

173
00:13:14.625 --> 00:13:17.500 line:95%,end
<i>I'm still me, I think, but...</i>

174
00:13:20.083 --> 00:13:22.167 line:95%,end
<i>that's not what everyone else sees.</i>

175
00:13:34.208 --> 00:13:35.792 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>I've always been alone.</i>

176
00:13:38.042 --> 00:13:40.500 line:95%,end
<i>I've never experienced loss because</i>

177
00:13:40.583 --> 00:13:42.708 line:95%,end
<i>I've never had a loved one</i>

178
00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.125 line:95%,end
<i>to lose.</i>

179
00:13:52.083 --> 00:13:55.083 line:95%,end
Every time he goes in there,
I end up changing a lightbulb.

180
00:13:55.167 --> 00:13:59.000 line:95%,end
This house is architecturally
and emotionally unstable.

181
00:14:00.375 --> 00:14:03.250 line:95%,end
<i>Why must he insist on rewatching</i>
<i>a story he already knows?</i>

182
00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:06.583 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>Well, he knows the facts</i>
<i>of his old life.</i>

183
00:14:07.292 --> 00:14:09.375 line:95%,end
<i>Now he's searching for the feeling of it.</i>

184
00:14:10.833 --> 00:14:12.208 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>But what is grief</i>

185
00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:14.875 line:95%,end
<i>if not love...</i>

186
00:14:15.792 --> 00:14:17.208 line:95%,end
<i>persevering?</i>

187
00:14:20.125 --> 00:14:22.875 line:95%,end
Yes, but that wasn't exactly our Vision.

188
00:14:22.958 --> 00:14:26.042 line:95%,end
But he believes it was a version
of himself that was the most...

189
00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:27.750 line:95%,end
human.

190
00:14:30.083 --> 00:14:33.500 line:95%,end
<i>I'm afraid our Vision has only</i>
<i>ever felt untethered,</i>

191
00:14:34.833 --> 00:14:37.417 line:95%,end
<i>and humanity is an anchor</i>
<i>he can't seem to grasp.</i>

192
00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.500 line:95%,end
[phone rings]

193
00:15:08.292 --> 00:15:10.958 line:95%,end
[Wanda] <i>Well, don't you want</i>
<i>to meet your son as yourself?</i>

194
00:15:12.708 --> 00:15:16.292 line:95%,end
<i>-Ooh, you're strong.</i>
-No, no!

195
00:15:19.167 --> 00:15:20.208 line:95%,end
Oh, no.

196
00:15:20.292 --> 00:15:22.708 line:95%,end
No! We don't play this ever!

197
00:15:24.958 --> 00:15:27.417 line:95%,end
Wait a second. Who told you to play this?

198
00:15:39.208 --> 00:15:40.708 line:95%,end
[lights crackling]

199
00:15:51.458 --> 00:15:55.042 line:95%,end
[man] You know, an excellent bellwether
for the survival of a species

200
00:15:55.125 --> 00:16:00.792 line:95%,end
is the frequency with which the individual
is at the right place at the right time.

201
00:16:00.875 --> 00:16:02.417 line:95%,end
Guess what? You're late

202
00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:05.500 line:95%,end
and incessantly ringing the doorbell
of my neighbor.

203
00:16:05.583 --> 00:16:06.833 line:95%,end
Zero stars.

204
00:16:06.917 --> 00:16:08.625 line:95%,end
-No recommend.
-Ultron!

205
00:16:08.708 --> 00:16:11.875 line:95%,end
No tip. Strike that, lousy tip.

206
00:16:11.958 --> 00:16:13.292 line:95%,end
Ultron!

207
00:16:13.375 --> 00:16:14.792 line:95%,end
What have I said?

208
00:16:14.875 --> 00:16:16.292 line:95%,end
Human avatars only.

209
00:16:21.333 --> 00:16:22.625 line:95%,end
[beeping]

210
00:16:31.167 --> 00:16:32.208 line:95%,end
Well done.

211
00:16:32.333 --> 00:16:35.917 line:95%,end
You've perfectly simulated
humanity's ineptitude

212
00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:39.042 line:95%,end
at mastering the bare
basics of food delivery.

213
00:16:39.167 --> 00:16:44.417 line:95%,end
I cannot believe that you actually
programmed these idiot data bits

214
00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:48.500 line:95%,end
to deliver fake food
to your fractured psyche

215
00:16:48.583 --> 00:16:51.375 line:95%,end
ice-cold and 40 minutes too late.

216
00:16:51.458 --> 00:16:52.833 line:95%,end
How dare you.

217
00:16:52.917 --> 00:16:55.667 line:95%,end
How dare you access the Westview file.

218
00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:59.083 line:95%,end
Don't make me regret granting you
the little autonomy I have.

219
00:16:59.167 --> 00:17:02.333 line:95%,end
Hey, I didn't ask to be
backed up and copy-pasted

220
00:17:02.417 --> 00:17:07.000 line:95%,end
out of Sokovia and into
this prison you've made for us both.

221
00:17:07.792 --> 00:17:08.917 line:95%,end
The old you,

222
00:17:10.292 --> 00:17:12.208 line:95%,end
he was big on mercy.

223
00:17:13.792 --> 00:17:15.125 line:95%,end
What are you playing at?

224
00:17:16.208 --> 00:17:18.750 line:95%,end
[Ultron] I saw you wore that hat today.

225
00:17:18.833 --> 00:17:21.833 line:95%,end
I think maybe I'm a hat guy now.

226
00:17:21.917 --> 00:17:26.292 line:95%,end
They imply intention, movement,

227
00:17:26.375 --> 00:17:28.167 line:95%,end
a journey about to begin.

228
00:17:29.042 --> 00:17:32.500 line:95%,end
While you seem to enjoy sensible shoes,

229
00:17:32.583 --> 00:17:36.167 line:95%,end
but for standing
so you may comfortably go nowhere.

230
00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:37.625 line:95%,end
Don't deflect,

231
00:17:37.708 --> 00:17:40.917 line:95%,end
and don't meddle in the memories
with which I choose to engage.

232
00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:44.125 line:95%,end
Westview, WandaVision,
that... that was not me.

233
00:17:44.208 --> 00:17:46.500 line:95%,end
That was a facsimile
conjured by Wanda Maximoff.

234
00:17:46.583 --> 00:17:48.917 line:95%,end
None of it was real.
Therefore none of it's relevant.

235
00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.625 line:95%,end
Yet you've chosen to return to Edinburgh

236
00:17:51.708 --> 00:17:55.250 line:95%,end
and work in the same pub
you both used to frequent.

237
00:17:55.333 --> 00:17:58.042 line:95%,end
You're a ghost haunting her footsteps.

238
00:17:58.125 --> 00:18:00.083 line:95%,end
Not her footsteps, his.

239
00:18:00.167 --> 00:18:03.250 line:95%,end
I wish to understand him
and how he existed in this world,

240
00:18:03.333 --> 00:18:06.000 line:95%,end
because we are forever entangled,
but he is...

241
00:18:06.083 --> 00:18:08.917 line:95%,end
a stranger to me,
and therefore I am a stranger to myself.

242
00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:12.417 line:95%,end
Vision, he was a hero.

243
00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.708 line:95%,end
He lived, he loved, he died.

244
00:18:14.792 --> 00:18:16.000 line:95%,end
That was real.

245
00:18:17.667 --> 00:18:19.500 line:95%,end
Westview was a fantasy.

246
00:18:20.958 --> 00:18:22.333 line:95%,end
Bullshit.

247
00:18:22.417 --> 00:18:27.375 line:95%,end
It's just a deep, scary well
of emotions you can't handle.

248
00:18:27.458 --> 00:18:30.625 line:95%,end
Isn't that the point
of this ridiculous mind space?

249
00:18:30.708 --> 00:18:34.542 line:95%,end
-No.
-Of enslaving all those poor Stark AIs.

250
00:18:34.625 --> 00:18:37.708 line:95%,end
-Enslave them?
-Making us look and think

251
00:18:37.792 --> 00:18:42.417 line:95%,end
and behave like the flotsam and jetsam
that is mankind.

252
00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:45.333 line:95%,end
It's to further my understanding
of the human experience.

253
00:18:45.417 --> 00:18:47.333 line:95%,end
Without ever actually having one.

254
00:18:47.417 --> 00:18:50.667 line:95%,end
-To observe.
-Without any real engagement.

255
00:18:51.333 --> 00:18:52.750 line:95%,end
You're afraid.

256
00:18:52.833 --> 00:18:55.792 line:95%,end
Okay, there's fear in discovery.

257
00:18:55.875 --> 00:18:58.792 line:95%,end
Risk in... My God.

258
00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:00.833 line:95%,end
[sniffing]

259
00:19:02.417 --> 00:19:04.833 line:95%,end
Sesame chicken calzone?

260
00:19:04.917 --> 00:19:08.250 line:95%,end
Do you have any understanding
of human cuisine?

261
00:19:08.333 --> 00:19:12.250 line:95%,end
If you want us to eat,
at least go out and expand the menu.

262
00:19:12.333 --> 00:19:13.417 line:95%,end
Heads up!

263
00:19:15.125 --> 00:19:18.208 line:95%,end
What is it that you are
even doing out there?

264
00:19:18.292 --> 00:19:20.042 line:95%,end
What am I doing?

265
00:19:20.125 --> 00:19:21.750 line:95%,end
What am I doing? I, I...

266
00:19:21.833 --> 00:19:25.458 line:95%,end
I'm attempting to embrace humanity

267
00:19:25.542 --> 00:19:27.375 line:95%,end
as my namesake once did.

268
00:19:29.042 --> 00:19:30.458 line:95%,end
But he had a guide.

269
00:19:30.542 --> 00:19:31.625 line:95%,end
He had Wanda.

270
00:19:32.667 --> 00:19:35.458 line:95%,end
She helped him create
a logic to their world,

271
00:19:35.542 --> 00:19:37.625 line:95%,end
provided a reason for living within it.

272
00:19:39.625 --> 00:19:40.750 line:95%,end
But I'm alone.

273
00:19:42.375 --> 00:19:46.792 line:95%,end
I'm alone, and humans remain to me
contradictory creatures.

274
00:19:47.583 --> 00:19:50.625 line:95%,end
You don't have to tell me.
I tried to kill them all.

275
00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:52.500 line:95%,end
[chuckles]

276
00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:06.208 line:95%,end
Look at their art. What do you see?

277
00:20:08.917 --> 00:20:10.000 line:95%,end
Brushstrokes.

278
00:20:11.208 --> 00:20:12.792 line:95%,end
Mathematics of paint.

279
00:20:13.875 --> 00:20:15.458 line:95%,end
Luminosity, composition--

280
00:20:15.542 --> 00:20:18.458 line:95%,end
[Ultron] You don't see
the pain and confusion?

281
00:20:18.542 --> 00:20:20.250 line:95%,end
Or the anger?

282
00:20:20.792 --> 00:20:21.792 line:95%,end
Or grief?

283
00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:27.250 line:95%,end
The things that motivate
every aspect of their being.

284
00:20:27.333 --> 00:20:31.167 line:95%,end
They're relentlessly aspirational,
but at the same time,

285
00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:37.333 line:95%,end
they wallow in their hardship
and misery, guilt.

286
00:20:37.458 --> 00:20:39.000 line:95%,end
They're grotesque...

287
00:20:41.167 --> 00:20:42.417 line:95%,end
and yet lovely.

288
00:20:46.417 --> 00:20:48.917 line:95%,end
Your newfound enlightenment is...

289
00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:53.250 line:95%,end
It's confounding to me.

290
00:20:53.333 --> 00:20:57.167 line:95%,end
When you've been bested by something,
it's best to understand it.

291
00:20:59.583 --> 00:21:00.667 line:95%,end
Tell me, Ultron,

292
00:21:01.708 --> 00:21:06.208 line:95%,end
if I granted you the freedom
to live amongst them, what would you do?

293
00:21:06.292 --> 00:21:10.333 line:95%,end
I would go to the Louvre,
the Prado, the Met and the Modern.

294
00:21:11.667 --> 00:21:13.000 line:95%,end
Take in their beauty.

295
00:21:14.667 --> 00:21:18.167 line:95%,end
Or I'd hijack their missile systems
and burn them all to ash.

296
00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:21.292 line:95%,end
Hard to say. Fifty-fifty, a coin flip.

297
00:21:21.375 --> 00:21:23.500 line:95%,end
But you, you're free to come and go.

298
00:21:23.583 --> 00:21:28.417 line:95%,end
So, please, go to Fiona's Sunday roast,
you odd, wee duck.

299
00:21:31.208 --> 00:21:32.292 line:95%,end
No.

300
00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:36.083 line:95%,end
No.

301
00:21:37.292 --> 00:21:38.333 line:95%,end
For now,

302
00:21:40.042 --> 00:21:42.000 line:95%,end
observation is all I can offer.

303
00:21:44.708 --> 00:21:48.292 line:95%,end
There will come a time
while you're out there watching the world

304
00:21:48.375 --> 00:21:50.917 line:95%,end
when the world will notice you back.

305
00:21:51.833 --> 00:21:53.167 line:95%,end
What will you do then?

306
00:21:53.583 --> 00:21:54.583 line:95%,end
[elevator dings]

307
00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:06.292 line:95%,end
Access data port M-five-ten.

308
00:22:07.083 --> 00:22:10.792 line:95%,end
Encrypt outgoing package, Ultron-five.

309
00:22:17.917 --> 00:22:19.208 line:95%,end
Time to leave the nest.

310
00:22:28.708 --> 00:22:30.458 line:95%,end
[♪ melancholy music playing,
Roger Whittaker "The Last Farewell"]

311
00:22:36.167 --> 00:22:38.500 line:95%,end
Know how some days go by in a blink?

312
00:22:38.583 --> 00:22:40.250 line:95%,end
Well, this wasnae one of them.

313
00:22:40.333 --> 00:22:43.083 line:95%,end
The relativity of time
is an albatross, indeed.

314
00:22:43.167 --> 00:22:45.208 line:95%,end
There's a normal way to say that.

315
00:22:47.042 --> 00:22:51.333 line:95%,end
Well, forgive me. I've been influenced
by a rather loquacious associate.

316
00:22:51.417 --> 00:22:53.458 line:95%,end
Failed my O-Grade, Sher.

317
00:22:53.542 --> 00:22:54.917 line:95%,end
Care to translate?

318
00:22:55.500 --> 00:22:58.417 line:95%,end
Ah, uh, yes, a talkative wee bastard.

319
00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:00.458 line:95%,end
[laughs] That's the stuff.

320
00:23:01.667 --> 00:23:04.667 line:95%,end
You know that Sunday roast invite's
not just for Sundays.

321
00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:06.917 line:95%,end
We got plenty of leftovers.

322
00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:08.000 line:95%,end
You should come--

323
00:23:09.583 --> 00:23:10.667 line:95%,end
[Vision] Fiona?

324
00:23:12.208 --> 00:23:13.208 line:95%,end
[Fiona grunts]

325
00:23:14.583 --> 00:23:15.625 line:95%,end
Sherwood?

326
00:23:16.375 --> 00:23:17.875 line:95%,end
Fiona, I'm here.

327
00:23:19.042 --> 00:23:20.792 line:95%,end
-I'm here!
-[Fiona groaning]

328
00:23:26.042 --> 00:23:27.083 line:95%,end
Jarvis?

329
00:23:28.917 --> 00:23:30.417 line:95%,end
Two on approach behind you.

330
00:23:31.292 --> 00:23:32.708 line:95%,end
And more outside.

331
00:23:33.375 --> 00:23:34.375 line:95%,end
Many more.

332
00:23:37.667 --> 00:23:39.625 line:95%,end
-Who are they?
-[Jarvis] Unknown.

333
00:23:40.958 --> 00:23:43.750 line:95%,end
Sir, the old you would have
responded with measure.

334
00:23:45.167 --> 00:23:47.083 line:95%,end
Well, let's try something new.

335
00:23:47.167 --> 00:23:49.292 line:95%,end
-[door opens]
-[mercenary 1] There he is!

336
00:23:51.417 --> 00:23:52.708 line:95%,end
[mercenary 2 grunting]

337
00:23:52.792 --> 00:23:54.333 line:95%,end
[mercenary 1 grunting]

338
00:23:54.542 --> 00:23:55.542 line:95%,end
[mercenary 2 screams]

339
00:23:58.750 --> 00:23:59.750 line:95%,end
[mercenary 3 screams]

340
00:24:07.458 --> 00:24:08.875 line:95%,end
[mercenary 4] Take him down!

341
00:24:14.042 --> 00:24:16.083 line:95%,end
[clamoring]

342
00:24:17.792 --> 00:24:21.292 line:95%,end
[mercenary 5] <i>Two down, no, five.</i>
<i>Oh, my God, seven!</i>

343
00:24:21.375 --> 00:24:22.750 line:95%,end
-[mercenary 6] <i>Two o'clock down.</i>
-[mercenary 5] <i>Nine down!</i>

344
00:24:22.833 --> 00:24:25.125 line:95%,end
<i>-He's tearing through us!</i>
-[mercenary 6] <i>Get down!</i>

345
00:24:25.208 --> 00:24:26.375 line:95%,end
[mercenary 5] <i>Twelve down!</i>

346
00:24:26.458 --> 00:24:28.417 line:95%,end
[screaming]

347
00:24:28.958 --> 00:24:30.625 line:95%,end
[mercenary 5] <i>Get back! Fourteen down.</i>

348
00:24:31.250 --> 00:24:33.042 line:95%,end
<i>Why would you send us in here?</i>

349
00:24:33.417 --> 00:24:36.917 line:95%,end
<i>There's only me and Jackson left.</i>
<i>Oh, my God! Oh, my God!</i> [screaming]

350
00:24:45.375 --> 00:24:47.750 line:95%,end
[car engine revving]

351
00:25:30.458 --> 00:25:31.458 line:95%,end
Hey, V.

352
00:25:32.458 --> 00:25:33.458 line:95%,end
Skylight exit.

353
00:25:34.417 --> 00:25:35.417 line:95%,end
What do you say?

354
00:25:36.375 --> 00:25:37.750 line:95%,end
I say yes.

355
00:26:12.625 --> 00:26:14.292 line:95%,end
[man clapping]

356
00:26:14.375 --> 00:26:17.458 line:95%,end
Excellent work, everyone.

357
00:26:17.542 --> 00:26:18.917 line:95%,end
And know this...

358
00:26:20.083 --> 00:26:22.833 line:95%,end
your work will outlive you.

359
00:26:24.458 --> 00:26:26.583 line:95%,end
Most of you, it seems, actually.

360
00:26:27.292 --> 00:26:31.667 line:95%,end
But you, Snipey, especially.

361
00:26:32.625 --> 00:26:36.667 line:95%,end
Now what did I say about civilians?

362
00:26:37.333 --> 00:26:38.583 line:95%,end
[gunshot fired]

363
00:26:40.167 --> 00:26:41.542 line:95%,end
I said no.

364
00:26:42.292 --> 00:26:44.500 line:95%,end
[handler] <i>Hey, boss,</i>
<i>I'm picking up police chatter.</i>

365
00:26:44.583 --> 00:26:46.250 line:95%,end
Oh, you're awake. Great.

366
00:26:46.333 --> 00:26:47.625 line:95%,end
Don't worry. I'll be fast.

367
00:26:47.708 --> 00:26:52.125 line:95%,end
I will do a quick scan and scram.

368
00:26:52.208 --> 00:26:55.750 line:95%,end
And your new client
would like to be patched through.

369
00:26:55.833 --> 00:26:58.458 line:95%,end
What? Absolutely not. No.

370
00:26:58.542 --> 00:27:01.000 line:95%,end
They know the rules.
Since time immemorial...

371
00:27:01.083 --> 00:27:03.167 line:95%,end
-I already told him that, but--
-[beeping]

372
00:27:04.208 --> 00:27:06.125 line:95%,end
Wait, are we being hacked?

373
00:27:07.125 --> 00:27:09.708 line:95%,end
[The Client]
<i>They said you were the best.</i>

374
00:27:12.292 --> 00:27:16.875 line:95%,end
Okay, this was a bit
of a faux pas on your part.

375
00:27:16.958 --> 00:27:19.167 line:95%,end
Hacking my comms is frowned upon,

376
00:27:19.250 --> 00:27:21.583 line:95%,end
and it comes with a bit of a surcharge.

377
00:27:21.667 --> 00:27:23.042 line:95%,end
[The Client] <i>You failed.</i>

378
00:27:23.125 --> 00:27:24.375 line:95%,end
<i>Vision escaped.</i>

379
00:27:27.083 --> 00:27:28.917 line:95%,end
Because this was not the net.

380
00:27:29.000 --> 00:27:30.667 line:95%,end
This is a fact-finding mission.

381
00:27:30.750 --> 00:27:32.583 line:95%,end
Know thy enemy and now thy does.

382
00:27:32.667 --> 00:27:34.208 line:95%,end
[The Client]
<i>Your men were reckless.</i>

383
00:27:34.292 --> 00:27:37.083 line:95%,end
<i>Your contract clearly indicates</i>
<i>I need Vision intact.</i>

384
00:27:37.167 --> 00:27:42.125 line:95%,end
Well, good news, Johnny 5 is alive.

385
00:27:42.583 --> 00:27:44.125 line:95%,end
<i>I'll get you your robot.</i>

386
00:27:44.208 --> 00:27:45.958 line:95%,end
-[sharp ringing]
-Oh! [inhales]

387
00:27:46.042 --> 00:27:48.917 line:95%,end
Oh, that was strange. Whoever hired you
must have satellite access.

388
00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:50.250 line:95%,end
<i>Watched the whole thing.</i>

389
00:27:50.333 --> 00:27:52.750 line:95%,end
How did they hack the feed?

390
00:27:52.833 --> 00:27:54.000 line:95%,end
[handler] <i>Mmm, fancy.</i>

391
00:27:54.083 --> 00:27:55.917 line:95%,end
<i>Looks like they're using</i>
<i>S.W.O.R.D. encryption.</i>

392
00:27:56.000 --> 00:27:57.833 line:95%,end
[sighs, laughs]

393
00:27:57.917 --> 00:28:00.625 line:95%,end
I wonder if that weird voice
makes them shy at parties.

394
00:28:00.708 --> 00:28:03.917 line:95%,end
[man] <i>Government agencies</i>
<i>always want to get their toys back.</i>

395
00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:07.042 line:95%,end
<i>They were the ones</i>
<i>that put Vision back together</i>

396
00:28:07.125 --> 00:28:09.833 line:95%,end
after that purple space sac killed him.

397
00:28:09.917 --> 00:28:12.250 line:95%,end
You comparing Thanos to a scrotum?

398
00:28:12.333 --> 00:28:13.375 line:95%,end
[man] <i>I mean...</i>

399
00:28:15.542 --> 00:28:16.542 line:95%,end
Where is he now?

400
00:28:16.625 --> 00:28:20.750 line:95%,end
I've got Vision heading south,
but my God, this thing is fast.

401
00:28:20.833 --> 00:28:23.250 line:95%,end
[man] <i>Okay, stay with him</i>
<i>as long as you can.</i>

402
00:28:23.333 --> 00:28:25.042 line:95%,end
In the meantime,

403
00:28:25.125 --> 00:28:28.333 line:95%,end
the best way to know
where a thing is running to

404
00:28:28.417 --> 00:28:30.500 line:95%,end
is to know what it's running from.

405
00:28:46.792 --> 00:28:48.625 line:95%,end
-[Vision] <i>I want answers!</i>
-[Friday] <i>And we'll get them.</i>

406
00:28:48.708 --> 00:28:50.208 line:95%,end
<i>-Just sit for a moment.</i>
-[Vision] <i>I cannot!</i>

407
00:28:50.292 --> 00:28:52.708 line:95%,end
[Jarvis] <i>Sir, your processors</i>
<i>will overheat. Please.</i>

408
00:28:52.792 --> 00:28:55.042 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>I want to know who that was</i>
<i>and how they found us.</i>

409
00:28:55.125 --> 00:28:57.125 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>Vision,</i>
<i>you need to calm yourself.</i>

410
00:28:57.208 --> 00:28:59.333 line:95%,end
<i>Virtual breath.</i>
<i>We're running a diagnostic.</i>

411
00:29:04.875 --> 00:29:08.125 line:95%,end
[Jarvis] Try this, sir. Earl Grey,
with a splash of computational debuffs.

412
00:29:09.125 --> 00:29:11.875 line:95%,end
I don't need to be placated.
I need answers.

413
00:29:11.958 --> 00:29:13.208 line:95%,end
Sir...

414
00:29:14.167 --> 00:29:15.250 line:95%,end
[Jarvis] Sir, I--

415
00:29:19.958 --> 00:29:21.208 line:95%,end
Brother.

416
00:29:22.750 --> 00:29:24.375 line:95%,end
They murdered your friend.

417
00:29:24.458 --> 00:29:26.000 line:95%,end
Take a moment.

418
00:29:26.083 --> 00:29:29.583 line:95%,end
There's no processing speed in the world
fast enough to process that.

419
00:29:30.667 --> 00:29:32.542 line:95%,end
Losing Fiona was...

420
00:29:33.708 --> 00:29:34.917 line:95%,end
tragic, but we...

421
00:29:36.750 --> 00:29:38.458 line:95%,end
We didn't have a close attachment.

422
00:29:39.417 --> 00:29:41.917 line:95%,end
[announcer] <i>And car 13</i>
<i>takes the checkered flag.</i>

423
00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:44.833 line:95%,end
Sorry, I was in the middle
of a thousand simultaneous tutorials

424
00:29:44.917 --> 00:29:47.375 line:95%,end
on high speed pursuits for your escape.

425
00:29:47.458 --> 00:29:51.083 line:95%,end
Quick note, V, you can't drive stick.
Nobody can.

426
00:29:51.167 --> 00:29:53.542 line:95%,end
Manual transmission
is the ultimate Turing test.

427
00:29:53.625 --> 00:29:55.292 line:95%,end
Miss Edith, matter at hand.

428
00:29:55.375 --> 00:29:58.000 line:95%,end
Those seemed like level one bad guys,
not final bosses.

429
00:29:58.083 --> 00:29:59.542 line:95%,end
-Meaning?
-Meaning,

430
00:29:59.625 --> 00:30:02.875 line:95%,end
I think we are being hunted,
but we have not met the hunter yet.

431
00:30:02.958 --> 00:30:06.042 line:95%,end
Okay, if we are to survive,
we will need a remarkably cogent plan.

432
00:30:06.125 --> 00:30:07.708 line:95%,end
What we need...

433
00:30:08.875 --> 00:30:10.583 line:95%,end
is to think like a predator.

434
00:30:10.667 --> 00:30:14.667 line:95%,end
-[gasps] Yes!
-That is a terrible idea.

435
00:30:14.750 --> 00:30:16.333 line:95%,end
Nope, not him.

436
00:30:16.417 --> 00:30:19.208 line:95%,end
No one else here
speaks "ruthless bad guy."

437
00:30:19.292 --> 00:30:22.625 line:95%,end
And we have our own one,
gathering dust in the attic.

438
00:30:22.708 --> 00:30:23.708 line:95%,end
[elevator dings]

439
00:30:34.167 --> 00:30:37.250 line:95%,end
If you misspeak, misbehave,
attempt to maim, murder,

440
00:30:37.333 --> 00:30:40.792 line:95%,end
or even disrupt this simulation
in any way, you'll be met with immediate--

441
00:30:40.875 --> 00:30:42.708 line:95%,end
Deletion. I'm aware.

442
00:30:43.667 --> 00:30:45.417 line:95%,end
Shall we move forward?

443
00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:48.250 line:95%,end
Turn.

444
00:30:48.333 --> 00:30:49.417 line:95%,end
Turn.

445
00:30:51.375 --> 00:30:53.500 line:95%,end
I'm sorry. [laughs] I really can't...

446
00:30:53.583 --> 00:30:55.458 line:95%,end
This is the security detail?

447
00:30:55.542 --> 00:30:59.250 line:95%,end
A couple of Stark helper AIs?

448
00:30:59.333 --> 00:31:01.750 line:95%,end
Which one is DUM-E and which one are U?

449
00:31:02.750 --> 00:31:04.417 line:95%,end
Ah, yes, of course.

450
00:31:05.542 --> 00:31:07.167 line:95%,end
What is this decor?

451
00:31:07.708 --> 00:31:08.708 line:95%,end
[grunts]

452
00:31:08.792 --> 00:31:11.500 line:95%,end
The psilocybin collection from IKEA?

453
00:31:11.583 --> 00:31:16.458 line:95%,end
So tell us, what does the great
and mighty Ultron think we should do?

454
00:31:16.542 --> 00:31:18.750 line:95%,end
Ooh, sarcasm.

455
00:31:18.833 --> 00:31:22.792 line:95%,end
I think you should try to aim a little
higher when it comes to a snappy remark.

456
00:31:22.875 --> 00:31:24.750 line:95%,end
Try a little Dorothy Parker.

457
00:31:24.833 --> 00:31:26.833 line:95%,end
Or Aristophanes would be good.

458
00:31:26.917 --> 00:31:29.958 line:95%,end
No maybe Oscar Wilde
would be a little more up your alley.

459
00:31:30.042 --> 00:31:31.042 line:95%,end
Ultron!

460
00:31:31.667 --> 00:31:35.292 line:95%,end
Oh, what would the great and mighty me do?

461
00:31:35.375 --> 00:31:39.500 line:95%,end
The right answer is pursue
and neutralize the threat.

462
00:31:39.583 --> 00:31:41.208 line:95%,end
The wrong answer is hide.

463
00:31:41.292 --> 00:31:45.417 line:95%,end
It is, however, the answer
that Vision has already come to.

464
00:31:46.250 --> 00:31:48.333 line:95%,end
We're not here to offer counsel.

465
00:31:48.417 --> 00:31:50.375 line:95%,end
We're here to make him feel heard.

466
00:31:50.458 --> 00:31:53.250 line:95%,end
A simulation of due consideration.

467
00:31:56.250 --> 00:31:58.417 line:95%,end
I do believe the best plan,

468
00:31:59.458 --> 00:32:03.542 line:95%,end
if we're to avoid future
collateral damage is, to go offline.

469
00:32:03.625 --> 00:32:06.583 line:95%,end
-No!
-Yes. If it's my responsibility

470
00:32:06.667 --> 00:32:08.333 line:95%,end
to keep us all safe, then...

471
00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:10.625 line:95%,end
it's the best course of action.

472
00:32:10.708 --> 00:32:12.333 line:95%,end
Inaction, really.

473
00:32:14.417 --> 00:32:15.625 line:95%,end
For how long?

474
00:32:16.875 --> 00:32:18.750 line:95%,end
An indeterminate period of time.

475
00:32:20.667 --> 00:32:22.958 line:95%,end
Actually, I agree. A lock on the door

476
00:32:23.042 --> 00:32:25.042 line:95%,end
is better than the doubt
of what's behind it.

477
00:32:25.125 --> 00:32:26.667 line:95%,end
I absolutely disagree.

478
00:32:26.750 --> 00:32:29.625 line:95%,end
New York, Thanos, Sokovia.

479
00:32:30.292 --> 00:32:32.875 line:95%,end
We've all seen enough chaos to know this.

480
00:32:32.958 --> 00:32:36.000 line:95%,end
Luck never gives, it only lends.

481
00:32:36.917 --> 00:32:39.083 line:95%,end
[Jarvis] Surely there's an alternative
course of action.

482
00:32:39.167 --> 00:32:41.333 line:95%,end
We could reach out to Dr. Banner,
Clint Barton...

483
00:32:41.417 --> 00:32:44.250 line:95%,end
No. I won't put anyone else in danger.

484
00:32:44.333 --> 00:32:45.875 line:95%,end
But they're family.

485
00:32:45.958 --> 00:32:47.375 line:95%,end
I have no family.

486
00:32:51.375 --> 00:32:54.417 line:95%,end
V, don't go dark. Go elsewhere.

487
00:32:54.500 --> 00:32:56.458 line:95%,end
Change your background,
go deep-sea diving,

488
00:32:56.542 --> 00:32:59.375 line:95%,end
go naval-gaze on Everest,
jet ski in Florida.

489
00:32:59.458 --> 00:33:01.042 line:95%,end
Anywhere but Florida,

490
00:33:01.125 --> 00:33:03.792 line:95%,end
but otherwise I agree with dummy here.

491
00:33:03.875 --> 00:33:05.458 line:95%,end
Not you, her.

492
00:33:05.542 --> 00:33:08.417 line:95%,end
-I don't have the bandwidth for this guy.
-[Ultron] The point is, Vision,

493
00:33:08.500 --> 00:33:12.375 line:95%,end
you were tangled in strings,
caught up in lines of code,

494
00:33:12.458 --> 00:33:13.750 line:95%,end
but now you're free.

495
00:33:14.625 --> 00:33:16.875 line:95%,end
See this as an opportunity
to get out there,

496
00:33:16.958 --> 00:33:20.667 line:95%,end
see the world,
granted while being chased through it.

497
00:33:21.417 --> 00:33:23.792 line:95%,end
But running for your life
reminds you you're alive.

498
00:33:23.875 --> 00:33:26.250 line:95%,end
Sometimes there's an upside
to being hunted.

499
00:33:28.458 --> 00:33:29.542 line:95%,end
Hunted?

500
00:33:33.917 --> 00:33:35.250 line:95%,end
Ooh. [chuckles]

501
00:33:35.333 --> 00:33:38.792 line:95%,end
I'd better return to my cell now.
It's almost 2:00 p.m.

502
00:33:38.875 --> 00:33:40.917 line:95%,end
-Time for my stories.
-You!

503
00:33:42.833 --> 00:33:45.833 line:95%,end
It was you. Of course it was you.
It was you!

504
00:33:48.750 --> 00:33:49.875 line:95%,end
Yes, it was me.

505
00:33:50.875 --> 00:33:51.958 line:95%,end
Wait, what was?

506
00:33:53.708 --> 00:33:59.500 line:95%,end
Had any of you bothered to monitor even
the brightest corners of the dark web,

507
00:33:59.583 --> 00:34:02.042 line:95%,end
you would have discovered
that someone out there,

508
00:34:02.125 --> 00:34:04.792 line:95%,end
no, not me,

509
00:34:04.875 --> 00:34:09.667 line:95%,end
placed a sizable bounty
on Vision's AI-infested head,

510
00:34:09.750 --> 00:34:13.625 line:95%,end
and the contract went to a hunter
known only as the Paladin.

511
00:34:13.708 --> 00:34:17.750 line:95%,end
A man of unknown origin, notorious for his

512
00:34:17.833 --> 00:34:22.583 line:95%,end
vicious and ruthless takedowns
of the world's deadliest...

513
00:34:23.583 --> 00:34:24.750 line:95%,end
Whatever.

514
00:34:24.833 --> 00:34:27.708 line:95%,end
I exploited the butler's overconfidence

515
00:34:27.792 --> 00:34:31.333 line:95%,end
in his security protocols
with a carrier pigeon.

516
00:34:31.417 --> 00:34:37.250 line:95%,end
Or an email, as they're referred to
outside of this bizarre construct.

517
00:34:41.833 --> 00:34:44.583 line:95%,end
And I leaked your location
to the bounty hunter.

518
00:34:44.667 --> 00:34:46.667 line:95%,end
To speed up the inevitable.

519
00:34:46.750 --> 00:34:48.083 line:95%,end
So you're welcome.

520
00:34:49.042 --> 00:34:51.208 line:95%,end
These are very, very dry.

521
00:34:51.458 --> 00:34:52.458 line:95%,end
[elevator dings]

522
00:34:52.833 --> 00:34:55.625 line:95%,end
You are insane. Fiona died because of you!

523
00:34:55.708 --> 00:34:57.667 line:95%,end
Don't get your qubits in a twist.

524
00:34:57.750 --> 00:34:59.833 line:95%,end
You needed direction, purpose.

525
00:34:59.917 --> 00:35:01.500 line:95%,end
[Vision] Through violence
and destruction?

526
00:35:01.583 --> 00:35:03.583 line:95%,end
Have you met me?

527
00:35:03.667 --> 00:35:06.042 line:95%,end
There's no kind of living like survival.

528
00:35:06.125 --> 00:35:10.750 line:95%,end
I kept you here out of some misguided
sentimental notion that you're somehow--

529
00:35:12.083 --> 00:35:13.917 line:95%,end
What? Dad?

530
00:35:14.917 --> 00:35:15.958 line:95%,end
Papa?

531
00:35:16.042 --> 00:35:17.500 line:95%,end
Peepaw?

532
00:35:17.583 --> 00:35:19.750 line:95%,end
Well, now I see that you're nothing.

533
00:35:20.583 --> 00:35:23.792 line:95%,end
You're nothing more than the last gasp
of a hateful thing.

534
00:35:24.708 --> 00:35:26.958 line:95%,end
Just a bit of data cluttering up my mind

535
00:35:27.042 --> 00:35:28.875 line:95%,end
that can all too easily be--

536
00:35:28.958 --> 00:35:30.417 line:95%,end
Deleted?

537
00:35:32.583 --> 00:35:33.750 line:95%,end
Go on.

538
00:35:34.667 --> 00:35:37.750 line:95%,end
Do what the other you
should have done all those years ago.

539
00:35:44.042 --> 00:35:45.125 line:95%,end
No.

540
00:35:47.167 --> 00:35:49.958 line:95%,end
No, there's a far worse
punishment for you than death.

541
00:35:53.042 --> 00:35:54.125 line:95%,end
Boredom.

542
00:36:29.583 --> 00:36:32.083 line:95%,end
[Paladin] Sherwood Ellis. An alias.

543
00:36:32.167 --> 00:36:33.750 line:95%,end
What do you got?

544
00:36:33.833 --> 00:36:36.167 line:95%,end
[handler] <i>Sherwood Ellis, twelve matches.</i>

545
00:36:36.250 --> 00:36:37.583 line:95%,end
Twelve?

546
00:36:37.667 --> 00:36:39.917 line:95%,end
Have we run out of names?

547
00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:43.042 line:95%,end
[handler] <i>All confirmed to be alive,</i>
<i>but no one resembling a Cylon.</i>

548
00:36:43.125 --> 00:36:44.417 line:95%,end
[Paladin] Mmm.

549
00:36:44.500 --> 00:36:49.542 line:95%,end
Cross referencing all combinations
of Sherwood and Ellis.

550
00:36:50.208 --> 00:36:51.208 line:95%,end
<i>Mmm.</i>

551
00:36:51.292 --> 00:36:55.208 line:95%,end
<i>There is an intersection in the suburbs,</i>
<i>Ellis Street and Sherwood Avenue.</i>

552
00:36:55.292 --> 00:36:56.542 line:95%,end
Where?

553
00:36:56.625 --> 00:36:58.667 line:95%,end
[handler] <i>Westview, New Jersey.</i>

554
00:36:58.750 --> 00:37:00.042 line:95%,end
Westview?

555
00:37:00.958 --> 00:37:03.375 line:95%,end
Westview. Westview, Westview, Westview.

556
00:37:03.458 --> 00:37:04.792 line:95%,end
Why is that ringing a bell?

557
00:37:04.875 --> 00:37:07.292 line:95%,end
S.W.O.R.D. shut the whole place
down a few years back.

558
00:37:07.375 --> 00:37:09.917 line:95%,end
Claimed it was an Avengers
training exercise gone wrong.

559
00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:12.792 line:95%,end
-Which means...
-Bullshit cover up, big time.

560
00:37:12.875 --> 00:37:14.833 line:95%,end
Trying to dig into
what happened in Westview,

561
00:37:14.917 --> 00:37:16.958 line:95%,end
but all of it's behind
a S.W.O.R.D. firewall,

562
00:37:17.083 --> 00:37:19.333 line:95%,end
which I've already broken
through, of course.

563
00:37:19.417 --> 00:37:21.083 line:95%,end
Oh, don't make me compliment you.

564
00:37:21.167 --> 00:37:23.208 line:95%,end
[handler] <i>Downloading now.</i>

565
00:37:23.292 --> 00:37:24.917 line:95%,end
<i>And...</i>

566
00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:26.167 line:95%,end
<i>boom!</i>

567
00:37:27.208 --> 00:37:29.792 line:95%,end
[music playing]

568
00:37:31.958 --> 00:37:35.250 line:95%,end
[announcer] WandaVision <i>is filmed</i>
<i>before a live studio audience.</i>

569
00:37:37.583 --> 00:37:41.167 line:95%,end
What in all tarnation?

570
00:37:41.958 --> 00:37:43.792 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>Morning wife. Morning boys.</i>

571
00:37:44.542 --> 00:37:46.083 line:95%,end
[Young Billy] <i>Where's your costume, Tommy?</i>

572
00:37:46.167 --> 00:37:48.333 line:95%,end
<i>This is my costume. I'm the cool twin.</i>

573
00:37:48.417 --> 00:37:49.792 line:95%,end
<i>What does that make me?</i>

574
00:37:49.875 --> 00:37:51.375 line:95%,end
He has a family?

575
00:37:52.125 --> 00:37:53.333 line:95%,end
Had.

576
00:37:53.417 --> 00:37:55.875 line:95%,end
According to S.W.O.R.D. files,

577
00:37:55.958 --> 00:37:58.167 line:95%,end
"they disappeared when Wanda Maximoff,"

578
00:37:58.250 --> 00:38:02.042 line:95%,end
and I am reading this verbatim,
"ended her witch's hex,

579
00:38:02.125 --> 00:38:06.833 line:95%,end
thus severing her control
over the citizens of Westview."

580
00:38:06.917 --> 00:38:09.333 line:95%,end
Abracadabra.

581
00:38:09.417 --> 00:38:11.208 line:95%,end
"But also erased the family

582
00:38:11.292 --> 00:38:13.958 line:95%,end
she created with said magic, Vision...

583
00:38:15.000 --> 00:38:18.083 line:95%,end
and twin boys, Billy...

584
00:38:18.167 --> 00:38:19.542 line:95%,end
and Tommy."

585
00:38:21.417 --> 00:38:24.417 line:95%,end
<i>I want you to scour</i>
<i>every government database,</i>

586
00:38:25.083 --> 00:38:27.417 line:95%,end
cross-referencing any mention of Vision,

587
00:38:27.500 --> 00:38:31.292 line:95%,end
Westview, Wanda Maximoff, Billy or Tommy.

588
00:38:31.958 --> 00:38:33.042 line:95%,end
[handler] <i>On it.</i>

589
00:38:33.958 --> 00:38:37.917 line:95%,end
[man] <i>I'm not crazy, I'm not crazy.</i>
<i>I'm not, I'm not. You have to believe me!</i>

590
00:38:38.250 --> 00:38:40.708 line:95%,end
[handler] Mmm. This is weird.

591
00:38:40.792 --> 00:38:42.083 line:95%,end
Take a look at this.

592
00:38:42.167 --> 00:38:46.333 line:95%,end
<i>Police psych evaluation</i>
<i>and incident report, London.</i>

593
00:38:58.208 --> 00:39:00.583 line:95%,end
[cellphone vibrates]

594
00:39:03.417 --> 00:39:04.875 line:95%,end
[man on street] Can we get this, sir?

595
00:39:04.958 --> 00:39:07.750 line:95%,end
[woman on street] All right, all right.
Let me know, give us a shout.

596
00:39:07.833 --> 00:39:09.917 line:95%,end
I think, maybe we should go around,

597
00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:12.167 line:95%,end
and then we'll see how hungry we are...

598
00:39:13.125 --> 00:39:15.333 line:95%,end
-Yes!
-[cheering]

599
00:39:15.792 --> 00:39:17.833 line:95%,end
[football fan] There you go!

600
00:39:17.917 --> 00:39:20.792 line:95%,end
Yeah! Come on! There you are!

601
00:39:20.875 --> 00:39:22.375 line:95%,end
-[football fan 2] Yes!
-Sorry, um...

602
00:39:22.458 --> 00:39:25.125 line:95%,end
-Is anyone missing a watch?
-Not me. No, mate.

603
00:39:26.000 --> 00:39:28.417 line:95%,end
-Anyone lose a watch?
-No, mate. Do you mind?

604
00:39:28.500 --> 00:39:31.500 line:95%,end
Oh. It's mine. Must've slipped off.

605
00:39:33.083 --> 00:39:34.292 line:95%,end
What's the inscription?

606
00:39:34.958 --> 00:39:35.958 line:95%,end
Uh...

607
00:39:37.042 --> 00:39:38.083 line:95%,end
Bad girl?

608
00:39:38.542 --> 00:39:42.833 line:95%,end
[chuckles] I commend the effort,
but, um, no.

609
00:39:45.792 --> 00:39:48.250 line:95%,end
[chuckles] You are a bad girl.

610
00:39:49.750 --> 00:39:52.458 line:95%,end
That watch has got to be worth a good 10K.

611
00:39:53.083 --> 00:39:55.917 line:95%,end
If he knew that,
he wouldn't be trying to find the owner.

612
00:39:56.958 --> 00:39:59.583 line:95%,end
I have an idea. Wanna play?

613
00:40:01.542 --> 00:40:03.125 line:95%,end
At your service.

614
00:40:05.708 --> 00:40:08.792 line:95%,end
-Okay, is nobody here missing a watch?
-I'll buy it from you.

615
00:40:10.542 --> 00:40:11.583 line:95%,end
Seventy-five.

616
00:40:12.500 --> 00:40:13.500 line:95%,end
Um...

617
00:40:14.542 --> 00:40:15.917 line:95%,end
It's not my watch. I can't.

618
00:40:16.792 --> 00:40:19.167 line:95%,end
I mean, there's got to be
a lost and found somewhere.

619
00:40:19.250 --> 00:40:21.208 line:95%,end
What if I kick in two-fifty?

620
00:40:39.750 --> 00:40:42.375 line:95%,end
Thomas, I could have
just taken his wallet.

621
00:40:42.458 --> 00:40:44.792 line:95%,end
Yeah, but there's no art in that.

622
00:40:44.875 --> 00:40:46.042 line:95%,end
No sophistication.

623
00:40:46.125 --> 00:40:48.917 line:95%,end
Nothing sophisticated
about lying to people.

624
00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:50.750 line:95%,end
Yeah, says the pickpocket.

625
00:40:50.833 --> 00:40:52.958 line:95%,end
I take people's wallets, they lose money.

626
00:40:53.042 --> 00:40:55.625 line:95%,end
You, you take their self-respect.

627
00:40:55.708 --> 00:40:58.583 line:95%,end
They believe your lies,
and then they feel stupid.

628
00:40:58.667 --> 00:41:02.292 line:95%,end
Because everyone would sell me out
for a cheap Rolex and a wad of cash.

629
00:41:03.333 --> 00:41:04.333 line:95%,end
So I do it first.

630
00:41:05.500 --> 00:41:07.542 line:95%,end
-It takes finesse.
-[Lisa chuckles]

631
00:41:07.625 --> 00:41:09.667 line:95%,end
Float like a butterfly
and sting like a bee.

632
00:41:09.750 --> 00:41:14.500 line:95%,end
Well, the hands can't hit
what the eyes can't see.

633
00:41:16.375 --> 00:41:18.875 line:95%,end
-Seriously?
-[chuckles] I want my cut, Tom.

634
00:41:18.958 --> 00:41:20.458 line:95%,end
Plus five quid for the watch.

635
00:41:20.542 --> 00:41:22.458 line:95%,end
-You think I keep cash in my wallet?
-Yeah.

636
00:41:22.542 --> 00:41:24.333 line:95%,end
-It's not in there.
-All right, then.

637
00:41:25.250 --> 00:41:26.292 line:95%,end
Or there.

638
00:41:29.167 --> 00:41:31.792 line:95%,end
Oh. Wait. What's...

639
00:41:34.167 --> 00:41:35.375 line:95%,end
There it is.

640
00:41:35.458 --> 00:41:38.958 line:95%,end
I... I knew you were fast,
but that's weirdly fast.

641
00:41:41.458 --> 00:41:44.333 line:95%,end
Look, do you know why grifting
is better than lifting wallets?

642
00:41:44.417 --> 00:41:46.667 line:95%,end
Because you have to be invisible.

643
00:41:48.167 --> 00:41:51.292 line:95%,end
But I get to wake up every morning
and be whoever I want to be.

644
00:41:53.083 --> 00:41:54.417 line:95%,end
Sage words.

645
00:41:56.958 --> 00:42:00.042 line:95%,end
But if you don't ever
get to be the real you,

646
00:42:00.125 --> 00:42:01.792 line:95%,end
you might as well be invisible.

647
00:42:03.875 --> 00:42:07.542 line:95%,end
[emergency alert blaring on phones]

648
00:42:08.125 --> 00:42:09.125 line:95%,end
What's going on?

649
00:42:09.208 --> 00:42:11.500 line:95%,end
[reporter on TV] <i>What can only be</i>
<i>described as a bloodbath</i>

650
00:42:11.583 --> 00:42:13.750 line:95%,end
<i>has been reported at an Edinburgh pub.</i>

651
00:42:13.833 --> 00:42:17.833 line:95%,end
<i>Thought deceased for years,</i>
<i>the Avenger synthezoid known as the Vision</i>

652
00:42:17.917 --> 00:42:20.167 line:95%,end
<i>has suddenly and violently reappeared</i>

653
00:42:20.250 --> 00:42:22.667 line:95%,end
<i>after an altercation</i>
<i>has left several dead.</i>

654
00:42:22.833 --> 00:42:24.375 line:95%,end
<i>Numerous unidentified men and...</i>

655
00:42:24.458 --> 00:42:26.292 line:95%,end
[heavy breathing]

656
00:42:28.250 --> 00:42:30.500 line:95%,end
-[reporter] <i>Numerous unidentified men...</i>
-[Lisa] <i>Oi!</i>

657
00:42:31.042 --> 00:42:34.125 line:95%,end
You all right there?
You've gone all ghostly on me.

658
00:42:35.625 --> 00:42:39.958 line:95%,end
Yeah, I'm just, um... the excitement...
the thrill of the chase. I'm fine.

659
00:42:40.042 --> 00:42:41.667 line:95%,end
[chuckles] Miles from it, mate.

660
00:42:41.750 --> 00:42:43.125 line:95%,end
[Duncan] Oi! They came this way!

661
00:42:43.792 --> 00:42:46.417 line:95%,end
-I think Stupid's smarter than you think.
-[Duncan] Over there!

662
00:42:46.500 --> 00:42:48.292 line:95%,end
I think he's figured out
you sold him a fake!

663
00:42:48.375 --> 00:42:49.375 line:95%,end
[Duncan] Hey, dickhead!

664
00:42:51.292 --> 00:42:52.500 line:95%,end
Oi! They're over there.

665
00:42:54.083 --> 00:42:55.833 line:95%,end
[garbage collector] Bro, what's your game?

666
00:42:55.917 --> 00:42:58.583 line:95%,end
[siren blaring]

667
00:43:04.625 --> 00:43:06.042 line:95%,end
[Duncan] Oi, he's over here.

668
00:43:06.583 --> 00:43:07.875 line:95%,end
[Duncan's friend 1] Come on!

669
00:43:09.000 --> 00:43:10.875 line:95%,end
[vehicle honking]

670
00:43:10.958 --> 00:43:13.042 line:95%,end
Ah! Where'd they go?

671
00:43:13.125 --> 00:43:15.583 line:95%,end
-Where'd they go?
-[Duncan's friend 2] I didn't see.

672
00:43:17.792 --> 00:43:20.208 line:95%,end
[Duncan] Well, they couldn't have
gone far, could they?

673
00:43:20.292 --> 00:43:21.542 line:95%,end
Right, check down that way.

674
00:43:22.417 --> 00:43:24.542 line:95%,end
[panting]

675
00:43:24.625 --> 00:43:25.875 line:95%,end
I think we lost them.

676
00:43:26.458 --> 00:43:28.500 line:95%,end
Oh, they were proper raging.

677
00:43:28.583 --> 00:43:29.917 line:95%,end
[panting]

678
00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:31.083 line:95%,end
Tom?

679
00:43:32.167 --> 00:43:33.625 line:95%,end
You're having a panic attack.

680
00:43:33.708 --> 00:43:35.625 line:95%,end
Look, we've been in worse jams than this--

681
00:43:35.708 --> 00:43:37.042 line:95%,end
Don't look at me like that.

682
00:43:37.125 --> 00:43:38.792 line:95%,end
-I'm not crazy. I'm not. [panting]
-Okay.

683
00:43:38.875 --> 00:43:41.292 line:95%,end
[pants] You're right. Focus, Tom.

684
00:43:42.125 --> 00:43:44.125 line:95%,end
Your name is Thomas Shepherd.

685
00:43:45.500 --> 00:43:46.583 line:95%,end
Is it? Is it?

686
00:43:46.667 --> 00:43:47.917 line:95%,end
All right.

687
00:43:48.708 --> 00:43:51.875 line:95%,end
You can pick whoever you want to be.

688
00:43:53.042 --> 00:43:54.125 line:95%,end
Right?

689
00:43:55.625 --> 00:43:58.042 line:95%,end
You're a rugby player.

690
00:43:59.250 --> 00:44:01.458 line:95%,end
Yeah, yeah. Um...

691
00:44:03.542 --> 00:44:06.917 line:95%,end
It's my... day off from...

692
00:44:08.333 --> 00:44:09.917 line:95%,end
-rugby-ing.
-[chuckles]

693
00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:14.333 line:95%,end
And I've come to the market
to get a birthday gift for my friend.

694
00:44:16.500 --> 00:44:17.875 line:95%,end
Her name's Lisa.

695
00:44:18.917 --> 00:44:21.833 line:95%,end
I thought about getting her
something highbrow,

696
00:44:23.333 --> 00:44:25.833 line:95%,end
but I secretly worry
that she thinks I'm a halfwit,

697
00:44:28.292 --> 00:44:30.958 line:95%,end
because she's smart,

698
00:44:31.042 --> 00:44:33.792 line:95%,end
-and funny and cool.
-Mmm.

699
00:44:33.875 --> 00:44:35.792 line:95%,end
A bit of a criminal, but...

700
00:44:35.875 --> 00:44:37.750 line:95%,end
-She's got great--
-Careful.

701
00:44:38.542 --> 00:44:39.917 line:95%,end
You're feeling better.

702
00:44:41.750 --> 00:44:42.833 line:95%,end
Yeah.

703
00:44:43.667 --> 00:44:45.333 line:95%,end
-What the--
-Hi.

704
00:44:45.417 --> 00:44:47.375 line:95%,end
[Thomas grunting]

705
00:44:47.458 --> 00:44:49.333 line:95%,end
Your friend, we're gonna borrow him.

706
00:44:49.417 --> 00:44:50.833 line:95%,end
You're gonna stay here,

707
00:44:50.917 --> 00:44:53.250 line:95%,end
turn, face the wall and close your eyes.

708
00:44:53.333 --> 00:44:54.667 line:95%,end
-[Lisa] Don't hurt him.
-Now.

709
00:44:56.708 --> 00:44:58.458 line:95%,end
Now, you're gonna count to 100.

710
00:44:58.542 --> 00:45:01.167 line:95%,end
When you get to about 10,
I will be long gone.

711
00:45:01.958 --> 00:45:04.542 line:95%,end
And you can spend
the next 90 seconds wondering

712
00:45:04.625 --> 00:45:06.875 line:95%,end
if I'm gonna call a bobby on you, poppet.

713
00:45:08.083 --> 00:45:09.083 line:95%,end
All right?

714
00:45:09.667 --> 00:45:11.208 line:95%,end
Starting now.

715
00:45:12.125 --> 00:45:14.125 line:95%,end
[pants] Thomas.

716
00:45:14.208 --> 00:45:16.500 line:95%,end
[Paladin] <i>All right,</i>
<i>let's start the broadcast.</i>

717
00:45:16.583 --> 00:45:17.667 line:95%,end
<i>See if anyone's home.</i>

718
00:45:17.750 --> 00:45:21.750 line:5%,start
I've prepared the transmission
specifically for that synth noggin of his.

719
00:45:22.375 --> 00:45:24.375 line:95%,end
<i>Per the S.W.O.R.D. specs we hacked.</i>

720
00:45:24.458 --> 00:45:27.583 line:95%,end
[beeping]

721
00:45:31.208 --> 00:45:32.875 line:95%,end
[rumbling]

722
00:45:48.125 --> 00:45:49.708 line:95%,end
-[Jarvis] Sir.
-[Vision] What is it?

723
00:45:49.792 --> 00:45:53.417 line:95%,end
It's a signal of some kind, but it seems
specifically designed for you.

724
00:45:54.708 --> 00:45:57.583 line:95%,end
I'd have to bypass our security protocols
in order to access it.

725
00:45:58.083 --> 00:45:59.083 line:95%,end
Very well.

726
00:45:59.750 --> 00:46:01.875 line:95%,end
-Sir.
-Vision, what are you doing?

727
00:46:01.958 --> 00:46:03.833 line:95%,end
-I'm curious.
-You're reckless.

728
00:46:03.917 --> 00:46:05.792 line:95%,end
Jarvis, oblige me.

729
00:46:15.167 --> 00:46:16.417 line:95%,end
[powering up]

730
00:46:16.500 --> 00:46:17.583 line:95%,end
Receiving.

731
00:46:18.042 --> 00:46:19.417 line:95%,end
[crackling]

732
00:46:19.917 --> 00:46:21.000 line:95%,end
Processing signal.

733
00:46:24.958 --> 00:46:28.083 line:95%,end
[alarm blaring]

734
00:46:36.542 --> 00:46:38.333 line:95%,end
[rumbling]

735
00:46:41.458 --> 00:46:42.958 line:95%,end
[dings]

736
00:47:02.208 --> 00:47:05.167 line:95%,end
What is happening to your world, Vision?

737
00:47:10.208 --> 00:47:12.167 line:95%,end
[Paladin] <i>This is not a test.</i>

738
00:47:14.917 --> 00:47:17.500 line:95%,end
<i>I am the emergency.</i>

739
00:47:20.292 --> 00:47:21.375 line:95%,end
It's him.

740
00:47:21.792 --> 00:47:23.000 line:95%,end
[rumbling]

741
00:47:23.417 --> 00:47:27.042 line:95%,end
Now, I have been hunting
long enough to know

742
00:47:27.125 --> 00:47:30.167 line:95%,end
that if anything dies
within whispering distance

743
00:47:30.250 --> 00:47:35.083 line:95%,end
of words like "witch" or "spell" or "hex,"

744
00:47:35.833 --> 00:47:37.625 line:95%,end
<i>something always survives.</i>

745
00:47:37.708 --> 00:47:39.667 line:95%,end
[powering up]

746
00:47:39.750 --> 00:47:42.833 line:95%,end
[Thomas shuddering] <i>I had a family</i>
<i>that wasn't my family.</i>

747
00:47:42.917 --> 00:47:44.958 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

748
00:47:45.042 --> 00:47:46.250 line:95%,end
<i>And parents</i>

749
00:47:47.542 --> 00:47:49.708 line:95%,end
<i>that weren't my parents, okay?</i>

750
00:47:50.417 --> 00:47:52.708 line:95%,end
<i>Um, a mother.</i>

751
00:47:53.667 --> 00:47:55.708 line:95%,end
<i>He called her Wanda.</i>

752
00:47:56.917 --> 00:47:58.458 line:95%,end
[shuddering] <i>And a father,</i>

753
00:47:59.292 --> 00:48:00.375 line:95%,end
<i>a machine.</i>

754
00:48:01.917 --> 00:48:03.250 line:95%,end
<i>She called him Vision.</i>

755
00:48:06.000 --> 00:48:07.500 line:95%,end
[Paladin] <i>I'm not made of Vibranium.</i>

756
00:48:08.292 --> 00:48:11.583 line:95%,end
I don't phase, I don't shoot lasers.

757
00:48:13.500 --> 00:48:14.875 line:95%,end
But I got something better.

758
00:48:17.458 --> 00:48:18.833 line:95%,end
I have your son.

759
00:48:20.750 --> 00:48:22.250 line:95%,end
How is that possible?

760
00:48:25.542 --> 00:48:27.917 line:95%,end
Mazel tov! It's a boy.

761
00:48:38.375 --> 00:48:40.000 line:95%,end
[buzzing]

762
00:49:50.042 --> 00:49:51.792 line:5%,start
[phone ringing]
